{
  "_comment": "fenton's SOUND v1 — lofi hip-hop, 75, A minor (Am7 Dm7 G7 Cmaj7). THE JOKE: the beat stays utterly calm while a man loses his dog. v2: the FULL 44.8s take plays once (fullfilm = exactly 14 bars at 75) with the kit rolling underneath — the original peace-to-chaos arc lands intact; the remix afterwards is the flip. v3: the film kit is a 14-step pick walk (one entry per bar) — the beat evolves WITH the take (peace/groove/run/OUT-on-jesus/sheepish return) while the video never cuts; film kit runs quieter than the remix kit so the take stays audible. v4: harmony + melody walk the take too — the progression itself is the 14-step walk (peace circle, E7 tension in the chase, dominant run, out on jesus, resolve home). Dusty swung kit (swing = @ elongation, long-short hats), one lazy pentatonic cell, chords drifting under a slow filter. The cries escalate against the chill; the STAMPEDE DROP chops the big run into percussion; jesus stops the world. Cries: HPF 180Hz (wind-blast stripped) then RMS-normalized to -16 with limiter — far-field screams have huge crest factors, peak-norm alone isn't enough (fenton's lesson, deepening Ron's). Beds raw. Moves spent: riff-bank walk + inhabit bass (oazoor), swing-by-@ (oazoor @ generalized), one-riff economy + filter-as-energy (switch-angel).",
